d an important part in social and <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">33</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t4-l-q33\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;changes.</li></ul><p><strong>Coffee and European colonization</strong></p><ul><li>European powers established coffee plantations in their colonies.</li><li>Types of coffee were often named according to the <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">34</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t4-l-q34\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;they came from.</li><li>In Brazil and the Caribbean, most cultivation depended on <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">35</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t4-l-q35\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>.</li><li>In Java, coffee was used as a form of <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">36</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t4-l-q36\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>.</li><li>Coffee became almost as important as <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">37</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t4-l-q37\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>.</li><li>The move towards the consumption of <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">38</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t4-l-q38\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;in Britain did not also take place in the USA.</li></ul><p><strong>Coffee in the 19th century</strong></p><ul><li>Prices dropped because of improvements in <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">39</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t4-l-q39\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>.</li><li>Industrial workers found coffee helped them to work at <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">40</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t4-l-q40\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>.</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":10}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/cambridge-ielts-13-academic-listening-4-audio-4.mp3"],"order_index":4}],"questions":[{"id":"en-c13-t4-l-q1","part_id":"en-c13-t4-l-p1","group_id":"en-c13-t4-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"Finance","correct_answer_variants":["Finance"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[1],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_12473_1","order_index":1,"points":1},{"id":"en-c13-t4-l-q2","part_id":"en-c13-t4-l-p1","group_id":"en-c13-t4-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"Maths/math/Math/maths/Mathematics","correct_answer_variants":["Maths","math","Math","maths","Mathematics"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[2],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_12473_2","order_index":2,"points":1},{"id":"en-c13-t4-l-q3","part_id":"en-c13-t4-l-p1","group_id":"en-c13-t4-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"business","correct_answer_variants":["business"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[3],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_12473_3","order_index":3,"points":1},{"id":"en-c13-t4-l-q4","part_id":"en-c13-t4-l-p1","group_id":"en-c13-t4-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","questi